    explanation: '"Inimical" means actively hostile or harmful to something, and it is the standard philosophical idiom for characterizing a methodology as working against its own stated purpose. Feyerabend\'s argument as described is not merely that standard scientific methodology fails to advance knowledge — it is that the methodology actively opposes such advancement by suppressing productive anomalies. "Inimical to the advancement of knowledge" captures this adversarial relationship precisely.',
